{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1f1dc01c0820dba305326130bbf571201bdaadab1e6d52f74cd6bec1699931f9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"sipyourdrink-ltd/bernstein@ce5c5217c1dc snapshot fa9ff58cd4c4ac48","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2cd4f91dbda5fb295b1aea81f43e6ecf8951552588b2ab6e9ed4d361301aebbc","slc_dc7d81c5e08d061f84eedd6df61bfeeed1e8d618960516241aaa53b4485a7a68"],"source_ids":["src_d9afc24621755158bfc599654af39cac"],"text":"The Task Server is a FastAPI REST application on port 8052 exposing /tasks, /status, and /metrics, with routes split across roughly 70 modules in core/routes/ and state checkpointed to .sdd/runtime/tasks.jsonl.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_24b48cfaf202ca21249154cfe5d376d482f770b9e5743a3908602581d21a96f9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"sipyourdrink-ltd/bernstein@ce5c5217c1dc snapshot fa9ff58cd4c4ac48","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_044329690cbdc2338ace880887d5e9acce548701897b0e57a33d9648c28d6ddd","slc_5f312b2bda37696139d7281a62ccfbcc1da342156adb2922f77947b9001c50b2","slc_7ffad65d6c9427c91fd2b6032aaa105c94cf5e6cd364bedc0f8feb2a4aa848dd","slc_e9421e739495df244942369162586c9158df3613176d7a52720ab25e7a248132"],"source_ids":["src_d129993ae9a751d88bad1c6df6a96bb0"],"text":"Runs are declared in YAML manifests defining phases, roles, node dependencies, conditional edges, and retry policies; workflow resume validates the manifest digest at start and refuses a changed spec.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_30baedf91f92c1f02efc97178cb0e217e8876fe0cc41365e146b423d57b5bc55","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"sipyourdrink-ltd/bernstein@ce5c5217c1dc snapshot fa9ff58cd4c4ac48","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0c140792164ed7964d37f521ec5bc18432d6cbacee7b1cf7687441fa8d606a6b"],"source_ids":["src_d9afc24621755158bfc599654af39cac"],"text":"A LineageSpine provides an always-on Merkle+HMAC provenance chain; every adapter artifact write routes through LineageSpine.record at a single write boundary, appending hash-chained rows to .sdd/lineage/<run_id>/spine.jsonl.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_587f4e0bee99f1d4a569b68b5914f1ab5d931735e118a675b35b9b3bbdc01b6c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"sipyourdrink-ltd/bernstein@ce5c5217c1dc snapshot fa9ff58cd4c4ac48","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0261b2b32aa1884a055c2ea3fc26119ef33269da546ccaa402549db74c3427ae","slc_a73b74e28a1eb57c457b5cdd2176c004d2b58a2797695409e258141057132066"],"source_ids":["src_d9afc24621755158bfc599654af39cac"],"text":"A janitor verifies task completion via concrete signals (files exist, tests pass, content matches) and moves tasks to done/ or failed/ without trusting agent claims; a separate LLM reviewer runs afterward and can push corrections back into the queue.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5d1e66f623075314a51fcf11be130f3b3b8a31bfd9796e1654645e763070de4f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"sipyourdrink-ltd/bernstein@ce5c5217c1dc snapshot fa9ff58cd4c4ac48","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9f54b09b5c45f70521c428a90e8af74ac3b037332e5cc9e29f565841251d1fb8","slc_dd0694a635d0a850968f78772067189c4d2b2974eab4a0e0d0a0c53b2059ba83","slc_fb74f88b1152c73d7e9921bc3707fb4407b6f47b752ba896bbfbcaae35eabe55"],"source_ids":["src_d9afc24621755158bfc599654af39cac"],"text":"All state is stored as files under .sdd/ with no databases or hidden memory, chosen for inspectability, recoverability, auditability, and git-friendliness; runtime state under .sdd/runtime/ is ephemeral.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_86720398fff7f344e1d1b38cfcd51aed69ca2788453df3828eba6e18d87da653","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"sipyourdrink-ltd/bernstein@ce5c5217c1dc snapshot fa9ff58cd4c4ac48","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4e175f6fa5cd1c99156a0dc2a8f039a95a4c2fa38eb0cb7f2d84218190cc189c","slc_692077097b031d4da9a2a6b798c2d3d4becc3cc0a1212cc8a846005e681740a6","slc_f0cb3c82bcd50c044f8d8c19a7c824e3ce589d30cbf0080ad68b434b29fabb9e"],"source_ids":["src_d129993ae9a751d88bad1c6df6a96bb0","src_d9afc24621755158bfc599654af39cac"],"text":"The orchestrator is deterministic Python with no model in the coordination loop; only one planning LLM call happens up front, and the same plan replays to a byte-identical task graph.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9a4dd64a7a3eecb1a0aed8ed6d90bf6af73529b3ec4bb9f4f62d3ec8b92780cb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"sipyourdrink-ltd/bernstein@ce5c5217c1dc snapshot fa9ff58cd4c4ac48","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_aa60883b635fc802c2c992b56130311c95038010b668cf665c647a6a90c10057"],"source_ids":["src_d129993ae9a751d88bad1c6df6a96bb0"],"text":"Volunteer compute tasks are constrained by a volunteer.json manifest declaring sandbox backend, network allowlist, and wall-clock/memory ceilings; a donor's own limits can only narrow, never widen, the declared containment.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_aacb4e5277f4c603c2fb561322cfad94c777f5c72965b6ee1da0bcf98c4c310d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"sipyourdrink-ltd/bernstein@ce5c5217c1dc snapshot fa9ff58cd4c4ac48","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5be18b865e66552feadd5e4284ba5bfcbce57d93027075e5a87de56c617a074c","slc_9624d864d46711a800f67c251373ebe5f5a2c2e45d9d1ec52a666db286e2f3b4","slc_d6e81a28c6ccbcd04b0a4c1d8ea0cf03c82272ea76db661deb7e291abaa69267"],"source_ids":["src_d129993ae9a751d88bad1c6df6a96bb0"],"text":"The project is beta, solo-maintained, and under active development; minor versions may change interfaces, and users are advised to pin versions. The volunteer one-command runner and the hosted api.bernstein.run service are not yet available.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bfc7ebce5ce6e4415806c3018a6a5963ee577342abc517038d699d809e1e5a1e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"sipyourdrink-ltd/bernstein@ce5c5217c1dc snapshot fa9ff58cd4c4ac48","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_171d798ee5561c6ab9df5c4e54b17d261b019973f4cedca42735ca46bdec8c32","slc_1af9054e864a2f7bd6f87676ce565826190660bdb3521b1f3a403a86769f574e","slc_7151b621f92f6090c3ae395ce4f51289505a7d5fc4fb7a3e859bbb072d353567","slc_9333a7ebd5d5c187abb5ee46583b2c8c911e21aead2a550c6bfc745fc8aeb139","slc_960052aef64a6c561bc16573bb7570a643062333133c88e60f09d4f274d59be8"],"source_ids":["src_d129993ae9a751d88bad1c6df6a96bb0"],"text":"The CLI surface includes bernstein init, -g, live, run plan.yaml, stop, workflow run/resume, replay/lineage/audit verification commands, and bernstein verify receipt for offline receipt checking.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ec6127f7c96f95933f033be31f1faa794485ef1a6cda73a9abe39dbfc7e10088","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"sipyourdrink-ltd/bernstein@ce5c5217c1dc snapshot fa9ff58cd4c4ac48","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2d38df8ec4973c1b7bcfc05c16a32018bb1a2bdd85b184e1b82b4bb9ee70c9e8"],"source_ids":["src_d129993ae9a751d88bad1c6df6a96bb0"],"text":"bernstein bench run <suite> --reliability k (also spelled bernstein eval) runs each task k times under fixed coordination and reports a pass^k floor alongside pass@1, sealing the result in a signed receipt that can be re-verified offline.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","created_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f6f971e5b4d98701fbd3d303301d5dde08acb83da7ac3bfefdce9a5f55675b4c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"sipyourdrink-ltd/bernstein@ce5c5217c1dc snapshot fa9ff58cd4c4ac48","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a0585d6a05c8a36ccc23289bdcedfe44d5c8b44c3673d11e82f3ace36e69d29a"],"source_ids":["src_d9afc24621755158bfc599654af39cac"],"text":"Pluggable sandbox backends implement a SandboxBackend/SandboxSession protocol; first-party options are worktree (default), docker, e2b Firecracker microVMs, and modal serverless containers, with third parties registering via an entry-point group.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:21:54Z","updated_by_operation":"op_daba580b51694f77bb109a2ca40ec175"}
